From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:04:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwcontext_vulkan: wait on the CPU before mapping RADV frames
 to DRM

vulkan_map_to_drm() attaches a sync file for the frame's pending work
to each exported dma-buf and skips the CPU wait, relying on the
importer to honour the dma-buf's fences. On RADV that never happens:
RADV allocates exportable memory with AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_EXPLICIT_SYNC,
and amdgpu ignores the fences in a buffer's reservation object for
every submission on an explicitly synchronized buffer. An importer on
the same device gets the same buffer object, so a VAAPI driver reading
the frame does not wait for the sync file and can read it before the
Vulkan work has finished.

On RADV, wait on the CPU instead, as is done when no sync file can be
exported.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
index dd2117f8ede8217c8969c3840990f9387e85603d..d92a6a586208bd68c4849eead1e980f51164e9b3 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
@@ -4239,8 +4239,14 @@ static int vulkan_map_to_drm(AVHWFramesContext *hwfc, AVFrame *dst,
         goto end;
 
 #ifdef DMA_BUF_IOCTL_EXPORT_SYNC_FILE
+    /* RADV allocates exportable memory as explicitly synchronized
+     * (AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_EXPLICIT_SYNC), and amdgpu then ignores the fences
+     * in the dma-buf for every submission on that buffer, including those of
+     * an importer such as the VAAPI driver. A sync file attached to the
+     * dma-buf would not be waited for, so wait on the CPU instead. */
     if ((p->vkctx.extensions & FF_VK_EXT_EXTERNAL_FD_SEM) &&
         f->tiling == VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT &&
+        p->dprops.driverID != VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_RADV &&
         vk->GetSemaphoreFdKHR && vk->CreateSemaphore) {
         err = vulkan_drm_export_sync_fd(hwfc, f, fp, nb_sems);
         if (err < 0)
